From: sep-touchid draft <noreply@invalid>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0100
Subject: [DRAFT][PATCH] spi: apple: optional SIO dmaengine TX path;
 dmaengine: apple-sio: one-shot slave_sg

*** DRAFT - NOT COMPILED, NOT TESTED ON HARDWARE, NOT APPLIED.
*** PRIVATE PROJECT: never send upstream / to Asahi.
*** Base: linux-asahi tag asahi-7.2.12-3 (~/kbuild/src/linux-asahi-7.2.12-3),
*** produced with diff -u on copies; `patch -p1 --dry-run` applies cleanly.
*** Design, recommended out-of-tree test path and test plan:
*** docs/dma_spi2_design.md (sections 3, 4, 5).

apple-sio:
 - add device_prep_slave_sg: one coprocessor descriptor per sg entry,
   no wrap-around, vchan_cookie_complete on the last MSG_REPORT;
 - announce DMA_SLAVE and DMA_DEV_TO_MEM (odd channels are RX already);
 - fix desc_allocated size (2 bytes allocated for a 64-bit bitmap);
 - sio_synchronize also synchronizes the vchan tasklet.
 The cyclic path (dpaudio) keeps its behaviour.

spi-apple:
 - optional "tx" DMA channel from DT (dmas/dma-names); without it the
   driver behaves exactly as before (spi1/spi3 have no dmas);
 - can_dma only for 8-bit TX-only transfers >= dma_min (default 256);
 - DMA transfer_one follows the register sequence macOS uses on spi2
   (project trace C19): SIO issue, RXCNT=0/TXCNT=len, STATUS=0x400023,
   CFG mode DMA + FIFO_THRESH field 2, CTRL=0xd, wait SIO report,
   drain, CFG back to IRQ mode, CTRL=0;
 - refuses (fail closed) a transfer mapped to more than one sg entry.

Known unknowns: SIO channel config values (apple-sio hardcodes the
dpaudio ones: fifo/threshold/limit 0x800, timeout 0), STATUS bits 5/22,
SPI-side completion in DMA mode, SHIFTCFG bit 2. See design doc section 6.

---
